course: dictionary
lesson: 12189
title: Confer, two meanings in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Confer is a formal word with two main meanings. The clues in the sentence show you which one is meant. When people talk together to share ideas before they decide something, confer means to talk together.
explain: «The judges conferred before they chose the winner.» The judges talked together before making their choice. Ask yourself: what are they doing before a decision? That tells you confer means talk together and share ideas.
explain: The second meaning is about giving something official. «The university conferred a degree on her.» The university did not talk to her. It gave her a degree, which is an honour. So confer can mean talk together, or give an honour, title, right or prize. Check the other words to see which one fits.
fact: Confer means to talk together and share ideas before deciding something.
fact: Confer also means to give someone an honour, title, right or prize.
fact: Everyday words for the first meaning are talk it over and discuss.
fact: «The king conferred a title on the brave knight.» Here confer means gave an honour.
fact: In some quizzes the rule is «No conferring», which means teams must not talk together before they answer.
exercise: «The teachers conferred about the trip before they chose the place.» What does conferred mean here? | To lose the way home | *To talk together and share ideas | To give a prize to the best pupil | To run quickly to the bus
exercise: «The king conferred a title on the brave knight.» What does conferred mean here? | To ask the knight a question | To forget the knight's name | To argue loudly with the knight | *To give an honour or title
exercise: A quiz rule says «No conferring». What does this rule mean? | Your team must hand in the paper early | You must write your answers in pen | You must sing your answer | *Your team must not talk together before answering
test: «The friends conferred with their coach before the match.» What does conferred mean? | To give a medal to the coach | To wave to the crowd | To shout at the referee | *To talk together and share ideas
test: «The school conferred a prize on Maya for her science project.» What does conferred mean? | To talk about the project for hours | To copy the project | To lose the project | *To give a prize
exam: Which sentence uses confer to mean give an honour or title? | «The two doctors conferred about the patient.» | «The children conferred and then ran off to play.» | *«The mayor conferred the title of Honorary Citizen on her.» | «We conferred about where to go on holiday.»
